  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Data Record of Oceanographic Observation & Exploratory Fishing - No. 6, 1962",
  "description": "Meteorological observations: Every three-hour interval, covering the whole course. Data are not presented here in order to save the printing cost, they will gladly supply by direct communication upon request. - Hydrographic observations: at 52 stations throughout three cruises, 10-(1), 10-(2), 10-(3), covering depths from the surface down to 1000 meters. - Analysis of water samples: Chrorinity was estimated by titration method after from the cruise. - Plankton sampling: Vertical hauls with a fine mesh net, 30 cm x 150 cm, XX 13 from approximately 100 meter depth, once at each hydrographic station. From approximately 150 meter depth, once at each hydrographic station. Horizontal tows with a larva net, 130 cm X 450 cm stramin, through the surface layer for ten minutes at low speed at hydrographic stations and other stations: - Fish Larva sampling: From the mixed plankton samples collected with a 130 cm larva net. - Salmon grill-net set: Twenty-four operations were carried out throughout three cruises at different stations. Specimens were used to the measurement of biological characters, observations on maturity, sampling of scales for later examination.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Purpose is to record of oceanographic observation & exploratory fishing - No.6, in March 1962",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23507017",
